{
  "Document": [
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Reactive State in Leptos"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "At the heart of Leptos is its fine-grained reactivity system. Unlike frameworks that re-render entire components (like React), Leptos only updates the specific parts of the DOM that depend on a piece of state."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Signals"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Signals are the primary way to manage state. A signal consists of a getter and a setter."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "CodeBlock": {
        "language": "rust",
        "code": "let (count, set_count) = create_signal(0);"
      }
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "InlineCode": "count()"
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Returns the current value."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "InlineCode": "set_count.set(val)"
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Updates the value."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "InlineCode": "set_count.update(|n| *n += 1)"
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Updates the value using a closure."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Derived Signals (Memos)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Memos are signals that depend on other signals. They are cached and only re-calculate when their dependencies change."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "CodeBlock": {
        "language": "rust",
        "code": "let double_count = create_memo(move |_| count() * 2);"
      }
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Effects"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Effects allow you to run side-effecting code (like logging or calling a JS API) whenever a signal changes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "CodeBlock": {
        "language": "rust",
        "code": "create_effect(move |_| {\n    logging::log!(\"Count is now: {}\", count());\n});"
      }
    }
  ]
}